>## Left-fold over a list with an Either-returning function, short-circuiting on Left.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>##
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## foldList(f, acc0, xs) folds f over xs from the left, threading an accumulator of type a, where each application may fail with Left e: it iterates while f returns Right, propagates Left on the first failure, and returns Right (final accumulator) if all elements were processed.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## Corresponds to a short-circuiting variant of Haskell's foldM specialised to Either.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## Renamed from hydra.lib.eithers.foldl, to distinguish the monadic fold from the plain list fold hydra.lib.lists.foldl.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>##
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## @availableSince 0.17.6
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra keyword.other.documentation.directive.hydra
#                  ^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## @requirement foldsLeftShortCircuitingOnLeft foldList folds the given function over the list from the left, threading an accumulator through successive right results; the first left result returned by the step function short-circuits the whole fold to that left, and folding the empty list returns right of the initial accumulator unchanged.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#   ^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra keyword.other.documentation.directive.hydra
#               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>primitive foldList : ∀x,y,z.(x → y → either<z, x>) → x → list<y> → either<z, x> = λf.λacc0.λxs.hydra.core.lib.lists.foldl (λacc.λel.hydra.core.lib.eithers.bind acc (λa.f a el)) right(acc0) xs
